SUPERSEDED, NOT SENT (19 Oct 2026): fixed upstream by f07317a8d57f
("scsi: ufs: ufs-qcom: Enable only lane clocks in lane clock APIs"),
queued for 7.4. See docs/power.md. Kept for reference only.

From: Nicola Nicodemo <nicola084@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: Don't enable the lane clocks twice

ufs_qcom_disable_lane_clks() returns early when the lane clocks are
already off, but ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks() lost the matching check when
it was converted to the clk_bulk API. Since the ungate path of
ufs_qcom_setup_clocks() also enables the lane clocks while the link is in
hibern8, overlapping calls (with ufs_qcom_hce_enable_notify() and
ufs_qcom_resume()) take references that are never dropped.

The bulk covers every clock of the controller node, ref_clk included. On
X1E80100 (Samsung Galaxy Book4 Edge) that is an RPMh clock buffer whose
enable count only grows (42 after 20 minutes of uptime, 110 after a few
hours, increasing across system suspend), so its vote can never be
released. With this change the count stays flat across suspend/resume.

Return early when the clocks are already enabled, as the disable path does.

Fixes: 9caef8568831 ("scsi: ufs: qcom: Use clk_bulk APIs for managing lane clocks")
Fixes: c1553fc105df ("scsi: ufs: ufs-qcom: Disable lane clocks during phy hibern8")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -356,6 +356,9 @@ static int ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks(struct ufs_qcom_host *host)
 {
 	int err;
 
+	if (host->is_lane_clks_enabled)
+		return 0;
+
 	err = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(host->num_clks, host->clks);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
